Verification, validation and a meaningful stress result (@mech-structural-verification: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "../study/Advanced-study-of-a-thermally-loaded-precision-structure.lingua#r_329Y297RYRM63KXKS3S1164SW3", #mechanical-engineering "../study/Advanced-study-of-component-fatigue-and-damage-tolerance.lingua#r_2AAKGM024C5C8GZ18EB2BCVPN7", #mechanical-engineering "../study/Advanced-study-of-material-models-and-nonlinear-structures.lingua#r_4ECSQ4X6CYDTGR4QFZSXJCBVGP") { r_4Z0234631TP38BBV5E4CZSE6A3
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Finite Element Analysis and Experimental Solutions; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), chapters 7–8 and the relevant exact solutions in chapters 4–5.

Verify the equations and numerical implementation against independent cases before interpreting a new component. Check units, coordinate frames, load resultants, reaction balance, energy, boundary conditions and limits. A patch test examines whether a simple exact field is reproduced; mesh refinement examines discretization behavior for a specified observable.

State whether the result is a nodal displacement, average section force, stress at an integration point, extrapolated surface value or singular idealized peak. Refining around a mathematical singularity can increase a plotted maximum without converging to a finite physical value. A meaningful comparison may instead concern a displacement, energy-release rate or stress away from the singularity.

Validate the physical model against independent observations with uncertainty. Fitting material parameters and then comparing against the same data is weaker evidence than a successful prediction under a changed load or geometry. Include plausible alternative support and material models rather than only increasing mesh density.

**Work:** Produce a convergence study for the original bar and one beam or plate case. Separate solver tolerance, discretization, geometric approximation, material uncertainty and measured boundary uncertainty. Identify a result that is numerically converged but physically wrong, explain how an observation exposes it, and revise the model.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
